WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let me start by thanking you
for being here

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.037 line:92%
and also congratulating you.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your wife gave birth
three days ago!

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She did.
-Congratulations!

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.377 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm a very, very,
very proud father.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I gotta say.
-Yeah. As well you should be.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was your second?
-My second.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I'm about to have
my second any day now, really,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.855 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and I have to say --

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.189 line:92%
Was the experience the same

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.060
or did you feel like a pro
being in there the second time?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Pbbht.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.096 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I mean -- Oh, I mean --

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
45 minutes
my wife took to deliver.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it was incredible.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
The nurses
were just extraordinary,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.405 line:92%
and I was in a state of shock.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.106 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I mean, I really was.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.443
-I only hope I can be as useless
as I was last time.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, really,
I was sending texts.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.582
And then the nurse -- When they
measured her cervix, they said,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.384 line:92%
"We're at 9. We're going."

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"We're what?"

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it was like --
Literally.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.758
-By the way, even at 8,
you shouldn't be texting.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.561
-[ Laughs ] But that was the
first measurement they took.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, oh, I got it.
-It was the first measurement.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.131 line:92%
We were there taking it easy,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it was like,
"We're 9."

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just like,
"Oh. Whoa. Okay."

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:09.736 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Well, that's great.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was it a boy, girl?
What'd you have?

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A boy.
-A little boy.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have another little boy,
as well, right?

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.875 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's very exciting.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
And may I just say
thank you to your family

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.015
for letting you be here tonight.
I really appreciate it.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.150 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thanks, guys, really.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
Papa really is working, James.
I'm actually...

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know it looks like
Papa's just talking to a man.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, my son, my son
doesn't know what I'm doing.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says,
"Where are you going, Papa?"

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, somebody comes
to pick me up again.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I --
"It's two sleeps, two sleeps."

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that -- You mean
you'll see him in two sleeps?

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's wonderful.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.268
-So if you're still up watching,
here I am.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.136 line:92%
-[ Laughs ] There you go.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.371 size:81% position:41%
"This is the bad man
who took your father!"

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.706 line:92%
-It's him, it's him, it's him!

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to ask,
how much did you know,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.845 size:88% position:44% line:92%
one, about the Kennedys,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, two, about
this specific moment,

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
this Chappaquiddick moment,
before this movie?

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm like most people.
I thought I knew a lot.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.353
Like everybody, I thought
I knew a lot about the Kennedys.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought I knew
about American politics.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought I knew
about this incident.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then
when I read that script

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I got off the plane
and checked the facts,

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realized how little
I did know.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And, you know,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.367
I couldn't believe some of the
things I'd read in the script,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
such as, you know,
the asphyxiation

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, you know, lack of air
rather than drowning.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.840 line:92%
-Well, it's funny. I just --

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.610
I do want to explain, because
I think you had this moment

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.777 size:84% position:42% line:92%
happen at the premiere,

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you realize
a lot of younger people

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't know about this moment
where Ted Kennedy
drove off a bridge.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a women in the car.
He survived. She didn't.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:36.556 size:78% position:39%
And this film kind of
covers the days after

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:39.759 line:92%
and his pretty terrible behavior

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the moments
after this accident happened.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, his behavior,
I mean, society's behavior.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you know,
he not only got away with it,

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.836 line:92%
but he also managed to thrive

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.639
and also went on to do a great
many wonderful, amazing things

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of the legislation
that he passed,

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.042 line:92%
and contribute to society.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.945
But, yes, he got away with it,
you know, and we elected him.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we talk now --
You know, obviously,

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the thing we're
talking about a lot right now

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.253
is what people in politics are
getting away with right now.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like nothing
we've ever seen before.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.692
And it does strike me that
current generations forget

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people have been
getting away with things.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not just people
in the Republican party,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
but people in the
Democratic party, as well,

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
with terrible behavior.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.935
-And did you find, like,
when you screened this --

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:24.204
Because I know one of the
taglines for the film is

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This really happened."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because people
might not believe

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this was a thing
that someone got away with.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's true. I mean,
things are pretty crazy now,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.145 size:78% position:39% line:92%
but 1968, you know --

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Martin Luther King. 50 years.
He was shot.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:35.949 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Bobby Kennedy was shot.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:38.384 size:88% position:44%
There were race riots.
There was a Vietnam War.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.819 line:92%
I mean, these are crazy days.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think
it's always important

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put things in context
and perspective

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and learn from history
and understand

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.760
that, you know what,
we've been through tough times.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.297
With the right people, with
the right thought and education

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:55.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
and votes and belief,
we can make better days.

